is its own reward.

263
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:31,460
And of course it's impossible to see

264
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:35,960
what is sound about that under the conditioned

265
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:37,960
situation in which he lives.

266
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:38,960
K. That's just an idea, sir.

267
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:42,460
A. It's an idea. So now we tuck that

268
00:21:42,460 --> 00:21:45,960
back, and then later when we need to remind somebody

269
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:48,460
that they are asking too much of a reward

270
00:21:48,460 --> 00:21:50,960
for something good that they did, we tell them,

271
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:54,960
well, have you forgotten that virtue is its

272
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:58,960
own reward? Yes, yes, it becomes a form of

273
00:21:58,960 --> 00:21:59,960
punishment.

274
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:07,460
K. So then, you see, seeing and hearing,

275
00:22:07,460 --> 00:22:14,960
then what is learning? Because they are all interrelated

276
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:18,960
– learning, seeing, hearing, action and all

277
00:22:18,960 --> 00:22:22,960
that. It's all in one movement. They

278
00:22:22,960 --> 00:22:27,960
are not separate chapters. It's one chapter.

279
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:30,960
A. Distinctions, no divisions.

280
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:42,460
K. So what is learning? Is learning

281
00:22:42,460 --> 00:22:53,960
a process of accumulation? And is learning non-accumulative?

282
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:55,460
We are putting both together. Wait

283
00:22:55,460 --> 00:22:56,960
a minute, let's look at it.

284
00:22:56,960 --> 00:23:02,960
One learns a language, Italian, French, whatever

285
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:08,960
it is, and accumulates words, and the irregular

286
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:12,960
words and so on, and then able to speak.

287
00:23:12,960 --> 00:23:16,960
There is learning a language and being able to speak.

288
00:23:16,960 --> 00:23:21,460
Learning how to ride a bicycle, learning how

289
00:23:21,460 --> 00:23:25,960
to drive a car, learning how to put together

290
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:29,960
a machine, electronics and so on and so

291
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:33,960
on. Those are all learning to acquire knowledge

292
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:40,460
in action. And I am asking, is there any

293
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:46,960
other form of learning? That we know. We are familiar

294
00:23:46,960 --> 00:23:51,960
with the acquisition of knowledge. Now is

295
00:23:51,960 --> 00:23:56,960
there any other kind of learning? Learning which

296
00:23:56,960 --> 00:24:04,960
is not accumulated and acting. I don't know if you...

297
00:24:04,960 --> 00:24:06,960
A. Yes, when we have accumulated it

298
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:08,960
all we haven't understood anything on that account.

299
00:24:08,960 --> 00:24:17,460
Yes. And I learn in order to gain a

300
00:24:17,460 --> 00:24:25,960
reward, or in order to avoid punishment. I learn a

301
00:24:25,960 --> 00:24:31,460
particular job, a particular craft in order

302
00:24:31,460 --> 00:24:36,960
to earn a livelihood. That is absolutely necessary.

303
00:24:36,960 --> 00:24:41,960
Otherwise... Now, I am asking, is there any

304
00:24:41,960 --> 00:24:46,960
other kind of learning? That is routine. That

305
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:50,460
is the cultivation of memory, and the memory,

306
00:24:50,460 --> 00:24:53,960
which is the result of experience and knowledge,

307
00:24:53,960 --> 00:24:57,960
that is stored in the brain and that operates.

308
00:24:57,960 --> 00:25:01,960
When asked to do, ride a bicycle, drive a

309
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:03,874
car and so on.

310
00:25:03,874 --> 00:25:04,374
拿

311
00:25:04,802 --> 00:25:11,322
Is there any other kind of learning, or only that?

312
00:25:13,602 --> 00:25:19,002
When one says, I have learnt from my experience,

313
00:25:21,082 --> 00:25:24,482
it means I have learnt,

314
00:25:24,482 --> 00:25:29,442
stored up from that experience certain memories,

315
00:25:29,442 --> 00:25:40,362
and those memories either prevent, reward, or punish.

316
00:25:43,922 --> 00:25:51,082
So, then all such forms of learning are mechanical.

317
00:25:53,922 --> 00:25:58,282
And the brain and education is trained,

318
00:25:58,282 --> 00:26:04,641
education is to train the brain to function in routine,

319
00:26:04,641 --> 00:26:11,162
mechanically, because in that there is great security.

320
00:26:14,561 --> 00:26:17,841
Then it is safe.

321
00:26:22,362 --> 00:26:27,882
And so our mind becomes mechanical.

322
00:26:29,042 --> 00:26:31,842
My father did this, I do this, you follow?

323
00:26:31,842 --> 00:26:34,322
The whole business is mechanical.

324
00:26:34,322 --> 00:26:41,162
Now, is there a non-mechanical brain at all?

325
00:26:41,722 --> 00:26:50,642
A non-utilitarian, in that sense,

326
00:26:50,682 --> 00:26:58,682
learning which has neither future nor past,

327
00:26:58,682 --> 00:27:01,122
therefore not time-binding.

328
00:27:01,122 --> 00:27:03,082
I don't know if I am making this...

329
00:27:03,082 --> 00:27:06,322
A.S. – Don't we sometimes say,

330
00:27:06,322 --> 00:27:09,482
I have learnt from experience,

331
00:27:09,482 --> 00:27:11,322
when we wish to convey something

332
00:27:11,322 --> 00:27:15,202
that isn't well conveyed by that expression,

333
00:27:15,202 --> 00:27:18,082
we wish to convey an insight

334
00:27:18,082 --> 00:27:20,882
that we don't feel can

335
00:27:20,882 --> 00:27:23,682
be, in a strict sense, dated?

336
00:27:23,682 --> 00:27:25,402
K.R. – Yes, sir. You see, sir,

337
00:27:25,402 --> 00:27:29,602
do we learn anything from experience?

338
00:27:31,362 --> 00:27:36,722
We have had, from history, history began, written history,

339
00:27:36,722 --> 00:27:40,122
five thousand wars.

340
00:27:40,122 --> 00:27:44,082
I read somewhere, five thousand wars,

341
00:27:44,082 --> 00:27:46,642
killing, killing, killing, maimed.

342
00:27:46,642 --> 00:27:49,882
And have we learnt anything?

343
00:27:50,762 --> 00:27:54,722
Have we learnt anything from sorrow?

344
00:27:54,722 --> 00:27:56,682
Man has suffered.

345
00:27:56,682 --> 00:28:01,202
Have we learnt anything from experience,

346
00:28:01,202 --> 00:28:06,402
the agony of uncertainty and all the rest of it?

347
00:28:06,402 --> 00:28:08,162
So when we say we

348
00:28:08,162 --> 00:28:09,922
have learnt, I question, you follow?

349
00:28:09,922 --> 00:28:12,042
It seems such a terrible thing to say,

350
00:28:12,042 --> 00:28:14,562
I have learnt from experience.

351
00:28:14,562 --> 00:28:16,962
You have learnt nothing,

352
00:28:16,962 --> 00:28:21,362
except in the field of knowledge.

353
00:28:21,362 --> 00:28:22,442
I don't know...

354
00:28:22,442 --> 00:28:27,161
A.S. – Yes, may I say

355
00:28:27,161 --> 00:28:31,881
something here that just passed in recall?

356
00:28:32,682 --> 00:28:36,122
We were talking about sorrow before,

357
00:28:36,122 --> 00:28:44,282
and I was thinking of a statement

358
00:28:44,282 --> 00:28:48,201
of St Paul's in his letter to the Romans,

359
00:28:48,201 --> 00:28:54,041
where there's a very unusual sequence of words,

360
00:28:54,041 --> 00:28:56,962
where he says, we rejoice in tribulations.

361
00:28:56,962 --> 00:28:58,001
Now, some people have thought

362
00:28:58,001 --> 00:28:59,041
he must have been a masochist

363
00:28:59,041 --> 00:29:01,362
or something in making such a statement,

364
00:29:01,362 --> 00:29:05,442
but that certainly seems to me bizarre.

365
00:29:05,442 --> 00:29:10,242
We rejoice in tribulations.

366
00:29:10,282 --> 00:29:14,562
And then he says, because tribulation works,

367
00:29:14,562 --> 00:29:18,082
and in the Greek this means that there's energy involved,

368
00:29:18,082 --> 00:29:21,761
works patience, patience experience.

369
00:29:21,761 --> 00:29:24,402
Now, that's a very unusual order,

370
00:29:24,402 --> 00:29:28,202
because we usually think that if we have enough experience,

371
00:29:28,202 --> 00:29:30,002
we'll learn to be patient.

372
00:29:30,002 --> 00:29:32,922
And he completely stands that on its head.

373
00:29:32,922 --> 00:29:38,322
And in the context of what you're saying,

374
00:29:38,362 --> 00:29:44,042
that order of his words makes eminent sense.

375
00:29:44,042 --> 00:29:45,082
Please go on.

376
00:29:45,082 --> 00:29:47,082
K. No, no, I'll go ahead.

377
00:29:47,082 --> 00:29:51,202
A. Yes, that's really very remarkable.

378
00:29:51,202 --> 00:30:00,082
K. You see, sir, that's why our education, our civilisation,

379
00:30:00,082 --> 00:30:02,281
all the things about us,

380
00:30:02,322 --> 00:30:06,922
has made our minds so mechanical,

381
00:30:06,922 --> 00:30:12,282
so repetitive reactions,

382
00:30:12,282 --> 00:30:17,202
repetitive demands, repetitive pursuits,

383
00:30:17,202 --> 00:30:20,962
same thing being repeated year after year,

384
00:30:20,962 --> 00:30:23,322
thousands of years,

385
00:30:23,322 --> 00:30:24,922
my country in your country,

386
00:30:24,922 --> 00:30:26,522
I'll kill you, you kill me.

387
00:30:26,522 --> 00:30:30,802
You follow, sir? The whole thing is mechanical.

388
00:30:30,802 --> 00:30:39,522
Now, that means the mind can never be free.

389
00:30:41,282 --> 00:30:45,042
Thought is never free.

390
00:30:45,042 --> 00:30:47,482
Thought is always old.

391
00:30:47,482 --> 00:30:50,442
There is no new thought.

392
00:30:50,442 --> 00:30:56,282
A. No, it's very curious in relation to a movement

393
00:30:56,282 --> 00:30:59,482
within the field of religion that calls itself,

394
00:30:59,482 --> 00:31:03,282
or did call itself, new thought.

395
00:31:03,282 --> 00:31:05,722
I was laughing at the irony of it.

396
00:31:05,722 --> 00:31:09,562
Yes, goodness me.

397
00:31:09,562 --> 00:31:14,082
Some persons, I imagine, would object to the notion

398
00:31:14,082 --> 00:31:16,522
that we don't learn from experience

399
00:31:16,522 --> 00:31:18,562
in terms of the succession of wars,

400
00:31:18,562 --> 00:31:23,082
because wars tend to happen sequentially,

401
00:31:23,082 --> 00:31:25,522
generation to generation, and you have to grow up.

402
00:31:25,522 --> 00:31:27,322
But that's not true, because wars,

403
00:31:27,362 --> 00:31:29,442
more than one war will happen very often

404
00:31:29,442 --> 00:31:30,721
in the same generation.

405
00:31:30,721 --> 00:31:32,682
K. Listen, what are they talking about?

406
00:31:32,682 --> 00:31:34,002
Two wars.

407
00:31:34,002 --> 00:31:36,721
A. Yes, hasn't been anything learned at all.

408
00:31:36,721 --> 00:31:39,642
At all.

409
00:31:39,642 --> 00:31:42,801
It's a terrifying thing to hear

410
00:31:42,801 --> 00:31:45,961
someone just come out and say,

411
00:31:45,961 --> 00:31:49,042
nobody learns anything from experience.

412
00:31:49,042 --> 00:31:52,521
K. No, the word experience also means to go through.

413
00:31:52,521 --> 00:31:54,122
A. Yes.

414
00:31:54,122 --> 00:31:55,322
K. But you never go through.

415
00:31:55,322 --> 00:31:57,442
A. That's exactly right.

416
00:31:57,442 --> 00:31:59,682
K. You always stop in

417
00:31:59,682 --> 00:32:01,922
the middle, or you never begin.

418
00:32:01,922 --> 00:32:03,922
A. Right.

419
00:32:03,922 --> 00:32:07,762
It means, if I'm remembering correctly

420
00:32:07,762 --> 00:32:10,762
in terms of its radical root,

421
00:32:10,762 --> 00:32:15,961
it means to test, to put to test,

422
00:32:15,961 --> 00:32:21,922
to, well, to put a thing to the test

423
00:32:21,922 --> 00:32:23,841
and behave correctly while that's going on.

424
00:32:23,842 --> 00:32:25,402
You simply have to. You

425
00:32:25,402 --> 00:32:26,962
see, you just have to look.

426
00:32:26,962 --> 00:32:28,162
Don't you?

427
00:32:28,162 --> 00:32:29,042
Yes.

428
00:32:29,042 --> 00:32:35,802
K. So, as our civilisation, our culture,

429
00:32:35,802 --> 00:32:40,842
our education has brought about a mind

430
00:32:40,842 --> 00:32:47,002
that is becoming more and more mechanical,

431
00:32:47,002 --> 00:32:49,522
and therefore time-binding,

432
00:32:49,522 --> 00:32:54,402
and therefore never a sense of freedom.

433
00:32:54,402 --> 00:32:56,722
Freedom then becomes an idea,

434
00:32:56,722 --> 00:33:00,882
you play around philosophically, but it's no meaning.

435
00:33:00,882 --> 00:33:02,982
But a man who says,

436
00:33:02,982 --> 00:33:05,082
now, I want to find out,

437
00:33:05,082 --> 00:33:07,642
I want to really go into this

438
00:33:07,642 --> 00:33:10,722
and discover if there is freedom,

439
00:33:10,762 --> 00:33:19,922
then he has to understand the limits of knowledge.

440
00:33:19,922 --> 00:33:23,362
Where knowledge ends,

441
00:33:23,362 --> 00:33:25,522
or rather, the ending of knowledge

442
00:33:25,522 --> 00:33:30,762
and the beginning of something totally new.

443
00:33:30,762 --> 00:33:32,162
I don't know if I'm conveying anything.

444
00:33:32,162 --> 00:33:33,922
A. You are. Oh, yes.

445
00:33:33,922 --> 00:33:37,721
K. That is, sir, what is learning?

446
00:33:37,721 --> 00:33:42,401
If it is not mechanical, then what is learning?

447
00:33:45,961 --> 00:33:50,842
Is there a learning at all? Learning about what?

448
00:33:53,241 --> 00:33:57,202
I learn how to go to the moon,

449
00:33:57,202 --> 00:33:58,882
how to put up this,

450
00:33:58,882 --> 00:34:00,562
that, and drive, and so on.

451
00:34:00,562 --> 00:34:04,521
In that field there is only learning.

452
00:34:04,562 --> 00:34:07,082
Is there any learning in any other field,

453
00:34:07,082 --> 00:34:12,042
psychologically, spiritually?

454
00:34:14,562 --> 00:34:20,161
Can the mind learn about what they call God?

455
00:34:21,362 --> 00:34:23,042
A. If in learning,

456
00:34:23,042 --> 00:34:26,962
in the sense that you have asked this question

457
00:34:26,962 --> 00:34:30,442
– no, I must rephrase that, stop this if-ing –

458
00:34:30,482 --> 00:34:34,842
when one does what I'm about to say,

459
00:34:34,842 --> 00:34:39,241
when one learns about God, or going to the moon,

460
00:34:39,241 --> 00:34:44,282
in terms of the question you've asked,

461
00:34:44,282 --> 00:34:48,641
he can't be doing what you are pointing to

462
00:34:48,641 --> 00:34:52,802
if this is something added on to the list.

463
00:34:52,802 --> 00:34:56,241
K. Sir, look, it's so clear. A. Yes, it is.

464
00:34:56,241 --> 00:34:58,042
K. I learn a language,

465
00:34:58,042 --> 00:35:00,522
ride a bicycle, drive a car, put a machine together,

466
00:35:00,522 --> 00:35:02,122
that's essential.

467
00:35:02,122 --> 00:35:04,662
Now, I want to learn

468
00:35:04,662 --> 00:35:07,202
about God. Just listen to me.

469
00:35:07,202 --> 00:35:11,562
God is my making.

470
00:35:11,562 --> 00:35:16,258
God hasn't made me in his image.

471
00:35:16,258 --> 00:35:17,238
Ha ha ha ha.

472
00:35:17,258 --> 00:35:21,258
I have made him in my image,

473
00:35:21,258 --> 00:35:25,258
and I am going to learn about him.

474
00:35:25,258 --> 00:35:27,258
A. Yes, I am going to talk to myself.

475
00:35:27,258 --> 00:35:31,258
K. Yes, learn about the image which I have built,

476
00:35:31,258 --> 00:35:34,258
about Christ, Buddha, whatever it is,

477
00:35:34,258 --> 00:35:37,258
the image I have built.

478
00:35:37,258 --> 00:35:39,258
So I am learning what?

479
00:35:39,258 --> 00:35:42,258
A. To talk about talk.

480
00:35:42,258 --> 00:35:46,258
K. Learning about the image which I have built.

481
00:35:46,258 --> 00:35:49,258
Therefore is there any other kind of learning

482
00:35:49,258 --> 00:35:53,258
except mechanical learning?

483
00:35:53,258 --> 00:35:56,258
I don't know if I...

484
00:35:56,258 --> 00:35:58,258
You understand my question?

485
00:35:58,258 --> 00:36:04,258
A. Yes, I do. Yes, I do. I certainly do.

486
00:36:04,258 --> 00:36:09,258
K. So there is only learning

487
00:36:09,258 --> 00:36:15,258
the mechanical process of life.

488
00:36:16,258 --> 00:36:19,258
There is no other learning.

489
00:36:19,258 --> 00:36:23,258
See what that means, sir.

490
00:36:26,258 --> 00:36:28,258
A. It means freedom.

491
00:36:28,258 --> 00:36:31,258
K. I can learn about myself.

492
00:36:31,258 --> 00:36:35,258
Because myself is known.

493
00:36:37,258 --> 00:36:40,258
I may not know it, but I can know

494
00:36:40,258 --> 00:36:45,258
by looking at myself I can know myself.

495
00:36:47,258 --> 00:36:53,258
So the myself is the accumulated knowledge of the past.

496
00:36:54,258 --> 00:36:57,258
The me who says, I am greedy, I am envy,

497
00:36:57,258 --> 00:37:00,258
I am successful, I am frightened,

498
00:37:00,258 --> 00:37:05,258
I am betrayed, I regret, all that is the me,

499
00:37:05,258 --> 00:37:09,258
including the soul which I have invented in the me.

500
00:37:09,258 --> 00:37:14,258
The Brahman, the Atman, it's all me still.

501
00:37:14,258 --> 00:37:18,258
The me has created the image of God

502
00:37:18,258 --> 00:37:20,758
and I am going to learn

503
00:37:20,758 --> 00:37:23,258
about God, which has no meaning.

504
00:37:23,258 --> 00:37:27,258
So, if there is...

505
00:37:27,258 --> 00:37:30,258
I am going to use the word if.

506
00:37:30,258 --> 00:37:36,258
If there is no other learning, what takes place?

507
00:37:37,258 --> 00:37:40,258
You understand?

508
00:37:40,258 --> 00:37:43,258
The mind is used in

509
00:37:43,258 --> 00:37:46,258
the acquisition of knowledge in matter

510
00:37:46,258 --> 00:37:48,258
– we'll put it differently –

511
00:37:48,258 --> 00:37:53,258
in mechanical things.

512
00:37:54,258 --> 00:37:59,258
And when the mind is employed there,

513
00:37:59,258 --> 00:38:05,258
is there any other process of learning?

514
00:38:06,258 --> 00:38:10,258
Which means psychologically, inwardly.

515
00:38:10,258 --> 00:38:12,258
Is there?

516
00:38:12,258 --> 00:38:15,258
The inward is the invention of

517
00:38:15,258 --> 00:38:18,258
thought as opposed to the outer.

518
00:38:18,258 --> 00:38:21,258
Right, don't you follow?

519
00:38:21,258 --> 00:38:23,758
If I have understood the

520
00:38:23,758 --> 00:38:26,258
outer, I have understood the inner,

521
00:38:26,258 --> 00:38:30,258
because the inner has created the outer.

522
00:38:30,258 --> 00:38:33,258
The outer in the sense of the structure, the society,

523
00:38:33,258 --> 00:38:38,258
the religious sanctions, all that is invented

524
00:38:38,258 --> 00:38:42,258
or put together by thought.

525
00:38:42,258 --> 00:38:48,258
The Jesuses, the Christ, the Buddhas, you follow? All that.

526
00:38:48,258 --> 00:38:53,258
And what is there to learn?

527
00:38:53,258 --> 00:38:55,258
A. In listening to you...

528
00:38:55,258 --> 00:38:56,258
K. See the beauty of

529
00:38:56,258 --> 00:38:57,258
what is coming out of it.

530
00:38:57,258 --> 00:39:00,258
A. Oh, yes, yes.

531
00:39:00,258 --> 00:39:05,258
It goes back to your remark about Vedanta

532
00:39:05,258 --> 00:39:09,258
as the end of knowledge.

533
00:39:09,258 --> 00:39:11,258
K. That's what I was told.

534
00:39:11,258 --> 00:39:14,258
A. Yes. The interesting thing to me

535
00:39:14,258 --> 00:39:18,258
about the Sanskrit construction is that

536
00:39:18,258 --> 00:39:20,258
unless I am mistaken,

537
00:39:20,258 --> 00:39:22,258
it doesn't mean the end of

538
00:39:22,258 --> 00:39:24,258
it as a terminus, as a term,

539
00:39:24,258 --> 00:39:27,258
because that would simply start a new series.

540
00:39:27,258 --> 00:39:33,258
It's the consummation of it, which is the total end

541
00:39:33,258 --> 00:39:38,258
in the sense that a totally new beginning is made

542
00:39:38,258 --> 00:39:40,258
at that very point.

543
00:39:40,258 --> 00:39:43,258
K. That means, sir, I know,

544
00:39:43,258 --> 00:39:47,258
the mind knows the activity of the known.

545
00:39:47,258 --> 00:39:50,258
A. That's right, yes.

546
00:39:50,258 --> 00:39:52,258
That's the consummation of knowledge.

547
00:39:52,258 --> 00:39:54,258
Of knowledge.

548
00:39:54,258 --> 00:39:58,258
Now, what is the state of the mind

549
00:39:58,258 --> 00:40:03,258
that is free from that, and yet functions in knowledge?

550
00:40:03,258 --> 00:40:06,258
A. And yet functions in it.

551
00:40:06,258 --> 00:40:12,258
Yes, yes. It is seeing perfectly.

552
00:40:12,258 --> 00:40:14,258
K. Go into it, you'll see,

553
00:40:14,258 --> 00:40:18,258
very strange things take place.

554
00:40:18,258 --> 00:40:22,258
Is this possible, first?

555
00:40:22,258 --> 00:40:24,258
You understand, sir?

556
00:40:24,258 --> 00:40:31,258
Because the brain functions mechanically.

557
00:40:31,258 --> 00:40:34,258
It wants security,

558
00:40:34,258 --> 00:40:36,258
otherwise it can't function.

559
00:40:36,258 --> 00:40:39,258
If we hadn't security,

560
00:40:39,258 --> 00:40:42,258
we wouldn't be here sitting together.

561
00:40:42,258 --> 00:40:47,258
Because we have security, we can have a dialogue.

562
00:40:49,258 --> 00:40:54,258
The brain can only function in complete security,

563
00:40:54,258 --> 00:40:59,258
whether that security it finds in a neurotic belief,

564
00:40:59,258 --> 00:41:01,258
or in a neurotic belief,

565
00:41:01,258 --> 00:41:05,258
all beliefs and all ideas are neurotic in that sense,

566
00:41:05,258 --> 00:41:08,258
so it finds it somewhere,

567
00:41:08,258 --> 00:41:14,258
in accepting nationality is the highest form of the good.

568
00:41:14,258 --> 00:41:18,258
Success is the highest virtue.

569
00:41:18,258 --> 00:41:22,258
That's all. It finds belief, security there.

570
00:41:22,258 --> 00:41:27,258
Now, you are asking the brain,

571
00:41:29,258 --> 00:41:36,258
which has become mechanical, trained, century,

572
00:41:36,258 --> 00:41:42,258
to see the other field which is not mechanical.

573
00:41:42,258 --> 00:41:47,258
Is there another field?

574
00:41:48,258 --> 00:41:49,258
A. No.

575
00:41:49,258 --> 00:41:51,258
K. You follow my question?

576
00:41:51,258 --> 00:41:56,258
A. Yes, that's what's so utterly devastating.

577
00:41:56,258 --> 00:42:01,258
K. Wait, wait. Is there another field?

578
00:42:01,258 --> 00:42:05,258
Now, unless the brain and

579
00:42:05,258 --> 00:42:09,258
the mind understands the whole field,

580
00:42:09,258 --> 00:42:13,258
understands the movement of knowledge,

581
00:42:13,258 --> 00:42:14,258
it is a movement.

582
00:42:14,258 --> 00:42:15,258
A. It's a movement, yes.

583
00:42:15,258 --> 00:42:17,258
K. It's not just static.

584
00:42:17,258 --> 00:42:20,258
You are adding, taking away, putting it, and so on.

585
00:42:20,258 --> 00:42:23,258
Unless it understands all that,

586
00:42:23,258 --> 00:42:26,258
it cannot possibly ask that other question.

587
00:42:26,258 --> 00:42:28,258
A. Exactly.

588
00:42:28,258 --> 00:42:31,758
K. And when it does

589
00:42:31,758 --> 00:42:35,258
ask that question, what takes place?

590
00:42:39,258 --> 00:42:42,258
Sir, this is real meditation, you understand?

591
00:42:42,258 --> 00:42:44,258
A. Yes.

592
00:42:44,258 --> 00:42:46,258
K. Which we will go into another time.

593
00:42:46,258 --> 00:42:50,258
So, you see, that's what it means.

594
00:42:50,258 --> 00:42:59,258
One is always listening with knowledge,

595
00:42:59,258 --> 00:43:04,258
seeing with knowledge.

596
00:43:04,258 --> 00:43:06,258
A. This is the seeing through a glass, darkly.

597
00:43:06,258 --> 00:43:08,258
K. Darkly.

598
00:43:08,258 --> 00:43:17,258
Now, is there a listening out of silence?

599
00:43:17,258 --> 00:43:23,258
And that is attention.

600
00:43:23,258 --> 00:43:26,258
And that is not time-binding,

601
00:43:26,258 --> 00:43:31,258
because in that silence I don't want anything.

602
00:43:31,258 --> 00:43:33,258
It isn't I am going to learn about myself,

603
00:43:33,258 --> 00:43:37,258
it isn't I am going to be punished or rewarded.

604
00:43:37,258 --> 00:43:43,258
In that absolute silence I listen.

605
00:43:43,258 --> 00:43:49,258
A. The wonder of the whole thing is that

606
00:43:49,258 --> 00:43:51,758
it isn't something that is

607
00:43:51,758 --> 00:43:54,258
done, this meditation, in succession.

608
00:43:54,258 --> 00:43:56,258
K. Sir, when we talk about meditation,

609
00:43:56,258 --> 00:43:58,258
we will have to go very deeply into that,

610
00:43:58,258 --> 00:44:01,258
because they have destroyed that word,

611
00:44:01,258 --> 00:44:05,258
these shoddy little men coming from India or anywhere,

612
00:44:05,258 --> 00:44:09,258
they have destroyed that thing.

613
00:44:09,258 --> 00:44:11,258
A. I heard the other day about someone

614
00:44:11,258 --> 00:44:16,258
who was learning transcendental meditation.

615
00:44:16,258 --> 00:44:18,258
K. Oh, learning. You follow the song?

616
00:44:18,258 --> 00:44:20,258
A. Of course.

617
00:44:20,258 --> 00:44:21,758
And they had to do it

618
00:44:21,758 --> 00:44:23,258
at three o'clock in the afternoon.

619
00:44:23,258 --> 00:44:27,258
K. Paid $35 or $100 to learn that.

620
00:44:27,258 --> 00:44:30,258
So sacrilegious.

621
00:44:30,258 --> 00:44:35,258
A. But if, that is, three o'clock in the afternoon

622
00:44:35,258 --> 00:44:39,258
was judgment day.

623
00:44:39,258 --> 00:44:43,258
If you didn't do it according to your schedule,

624
00:44:43,258 --> 00:44:46,258
then the world has obviously come to an end.

625
00:44:46,258 --> 00:44:48,258
But ostensibly you are doing

626
00:44:48,258 --> 00:44:50,258
it to get free of that.

627
00:44:50,258 --> 00:44:52,258
Do go ahead.

628
00:44:52,258 --> 00:44:56,258
K. So you see, sir, that is what takes place.

629
00:44:56,258 --> 00:45:00,258
We began this morning about beauty,

630
00:45:00,258 --> 00:45:06,258
then passion, then suffering, then action.

631
00:45:06,258 --> 00:45:11,258
Action based on idea is inaction.

632
00:45:11,258 --> 00:45:15,258
It sounds monstrous, but there it is.

633
00:45:15,258 --> 00:45:18,258
And from that we said, what

634
00:45:18,258 --> 00:45:21,258
is seeing and what is hearing?

635
00:45:22,258 --> 00:45:28,258
The seeing and the listening has become mechanical.

636
00:45:30,258 --> 00:45:33,258
We never see anything new.

637
00:45:33,258 --> 00:45:37,258
Even the flower is never new,

638
00:45:37,258 --> 00:45:39,258
which has blossomed overnight.

639
00:45:39,258 --> 00:45:40,758
We say, yes, that is the

640
00:45:40,758 --> 00:45:42,258
rose, I have been expecting it,

641
00:45:42,258 --> 00:45:46,258
it has come out now, how beautiful.

642
00:45:46,258 --> 00:45:52,258
It is always from the known to the known.

643
00:45:52,258 --> 00:45:56,258
A movement in time and therefore time-binding,

644
00:45:56,258 --> 00:46:00,258
and therefore never free.

645
00:46:00,258 --> 00:46:03,258
And yet we are talking about freedom,

646
00:46:03,258 --> 00:46:09,258
philosophy, the lectures on freedom, and so on, so on.

647
00:46:09,258 --> 00:46:11,258
And the communists call it

648
00:46:11,258 --> 00:46:13,258
a bourgeois thing, which it is,

649
00:46:13,258 --> 00:46:17,258
in the sense, when you limit it to knowledge,

650
00:46:17,258 --> 00:46:21,258
it is foolish to talk about freedom.

651
00:46:21,258 --> 00:46:24,258
But there is a freedom

652
00:46:24,258 --> 00:46:31,258
when you understand the movement of knowledge.

653
00:46:31,258 --> 00:46:39,258
So can you observe out of silence,

654
00:46:40,258 --> 00:46:45,258
and observe and act in the field of knowledge,

655
00:46:45,258 --> 00:46:50,258
both together in harmony?

656
00:46:51,258 --> 00:46:56,258
A.M. Seeing, then, is not scheduled.

657
00:46:56,258 --> 00:46:59,258
Yes, of course.

658
00:46:59,258 --> 00:47:02,258
What a...

659
00:47:02,258 --> 00:47:05,258
Yes, sir.

660
00:47:09,258 --> 00:47:14,258
I was just thinking about the...

661
00:47:14,258 --> 00:47:18,258
I suppose you would say a classical definition of freedom

662
00:47:18,258 --> 00:47:21,258
in terms of the career of knowledge,

663
00:47:21,258 --> 00:47:26,258
would be that it is a property of action,

664
00:47:26,258 --> 00:47:29,258
a property or quality of action,

665
00:47:29,258 --> 00:47:33,258
for general uses, either word would do,

666
00:47:33,258 --> 00:47:36,258
property or quality.

667
00:47:36,258 --> 00:47:39,258
And it occurred to me,

668
00:47:39,258 --> 00:47:43,258
in the context of what we have been saying,

669
00:47:43,258 --> 00:47:50,258
what a horror that one could read that statement,

670
00:47:50,258 --> 00:47:56,258
and not let it disclose itself to you.

671
00:47:56,258 --> 00:47:59,258
If it disclosed itself to you,

672
00:47:59,258 --> 00:48:02,258
you would be up against it.

673
00:48:02,258 --> 00:48:05,258
You would have to be serious.

674
00:48:05,258 --> 00:48:07,258
If you were a philosophy student and you read that,

675
00:48:07,258 --> 00:48:11,258
and that thing began to operate in you,

676
00:48:11,258 --> 00:48:13,258
you would say,

677
00:48:13,258 --> 00:48:14,758
I have got to get

678
00:48:14,758 --> 00:48:16,258
this settled before I go on,

679
00:48:16,258 --> 00:48:17,258
maybe I will never graduate.

680
00:48:17,258 --> 00:48:18,258
That is not important.

681
00:48:18,258 --> 00:48:20,258
K. That is not important, quite right.

682
00:48:20,258 --> 00:48:23,258
And I was thinking,

683
00:48:23,258 --> 00:48:26,258
in the West as well as in the East,

684
00:48:26,258 --> 00:48:29,258
you have to go to the factory or the office,

685
00:48:29,258 --> 00:48:36,258
the factory or the office every day of your life.

686
00:48:36,258 --> 00:48:40,258
Get up at nine o'clock, eight o'clock, six o'clock,

687
00:48:40,258 --> 00:48:45,258
drive, walk, work, work, work,

688
00:48:45,258 --> 00:48:49,258
for fifty years, routine,

689
00:48:49,258 --> 00:48:53,258
and get kicked about, insulted,

690
00:48:53,258 --> 00:48:58,258
worship success, again repetition,

691
00:48:58,258 --> 00:49:02,258
and occasionally talk about God if it is convenient,

692
00:49:02,258 --> 00:49:04,258
and so on and so on.

693
00:49:04,258 --> 00:49:09,258
That is a monstrous life.

694
00:49:10,258 --> 00:49:16,258
And that is what we are educating our children for.

695
00:49:16,258 --> 00:49:20,258
A. That is the real living death.

696
00:49:20,258 --> 00:49:22,258
K. And nobody says,

697
00:49:22,258 --> 00:49:24,758
for God's sake, let's look

698
00:49:24,758 --> 00:49:27,258
at all this, I am new.

699
00:49:27,258 --> 00:49:30,258
Let's wipe our eyes clear of the past

700
00:49:30,258 --> 00:49:33,258
and look what we are doing,

701
00:49:33,258 --> 00:49:36,258
give attention, care what we are doing.

702
00:49:36,258 --> 00:49:39,258
A. No, we have this question instead.

703
00:49:39,258 --> 00:49:41,258
What shall we do about it?

704
00:49:41,258 --> 00:49:43,258
Yes, that is the question.

705
00:49:43,258 --> 00:49:47,258
And then that becomes the next thing done.

706
00:49:47,258 --> 00:49:48,758
K. Which is the continuity of

707
00:49:48,758 --> 00:49:50,258
the past in a different form.

708
00:49:50,258 --> 00:49:52,258
A. And the chain is

709
00:49:52,258 --> 00:49:54,258
endlessly linked, linked, linked, linked.

710
00:49:54,258 --> 00:49:58,258
Cause becoming the effect and the effect becoming the cause.

711
00:49:58,258 --> 00:50:00,758
So it is a very serious

712
00:50:00,758 --> 00:50:03,258
thing when we talk about all this,

713
00:50:03,258 --> 00:50:08,258
because life becomes dreadfully serious.

714
00:50:08,258 --> 00:50:13,258
And it is only this serious person that lives,

715
00:50:13,258 --> 00:50:17,258
not these people who seek entertainment,

716
00:50:17,258 --> 00:50:20,258
religious or otherwise.

717
00:50:20,258 --> 00:50:23,258
A. I had a very interesting occasion

718
00:50:23,258 --> 00:50:29,258
to understand what you are saying in class yesterday.

719
00:50:29,258 --> 00:50:35,258
I was trying to assist the students to see that

720
00:50:35,258 --> 00:50:40,258
the classical understanding of the four causes in operation

721
00:50:40,258 --> 00:50:44,258
is that they are non-temporarily related.

722
00:50:44,258 --> 00:50:46,758
And I said when the potter

723
00:50:46,758 --> 00:50:49,258
puts his hand to the clay,

724
00:50:49,258 --> 00:50:51,758
the hand touching the clay is

725
00:50:51,758 --> 00:50:54,258
not responded to by the clay

726
00:50:54,258 --> 00:50:57,258
after the hand has touched it.

727
00:50:57,258 --> 00:51:06,258
And one person who was visiting the class,

728
00:51:06,258 --> 00:51:14,258
this person was a well-educated person

729
00:51:14,258 --> 00:51:19,258
and a professor.

730
00:51:19,258 --> 00:51:24,258
And this struck them as maybe not so.

731
00:51:24,258 --> 00:51:28,258
And I could tell by the expression on the face

732
00:51:28,258 --> 00:51:30,258
that there was this little anguish here.

733
00:51:30,258 --> 00:51:32,758
So I said, well, my radar says

734
00:51:32,758 --> 00:51:35,258
that there is some difficulty going on.

735
00:51:35,258 --> 00:51:37,258
What is the matter?

736
00:51:37,258 --> 00:51:41,258
Well, it seems like there is a time interval.

737
00:51:42,258 --> 00:51:44,258
So I asked them to pick

738
00:51:44,258 --> 00:51:46,258
something up that was on the desk,

739
00:51:46,258 --> 00:51:48,258
and I said, well, now touch it with your finger

740
00:51:48,258 --> 00:51:50,258
and tell me at the moment

741
00:51:50,258 --> 00:51:52,258
of the touching with the finger

742
00:51:52,258 --> 00:52:00,258
whether the thing reacts to the finger after it's touched.

743
00:52:00,258 --> 00:52:02,258
Now, do it.

744
00:52:02,258 --> 00:52:04,758
Well, even to ask somebody to

745
00:52:04,758 --> 00:52:07,258
apply a practical test like that

746
00:52:07,258 --> 00:52:10,258
with respect to a datum of knowledge,

747
00:52:10,258 --> 00:52:13,258
about the four causes, or...

748
00:52:13,258 --> 00:52:15,758
is to interrupt the process

749
00:52:15,758 --> 00:52:18,258
of education as we've known it,

750
00:52:18,258 --> 00:52:20,258
because you teach a student about the four causes

751
00:52:20,258 --> 00:52:22,258
and he thinks about them.

752
00:52:22,258 --> 00:52:24,258
He never goes out and looks at a thing

753
00:52:24,258 --> 00:52:26,258
or does anything about it.

754
00:52:26,258 --> 00:52:29,258
And so we spent about...

755
00:52:29,258 --> 00:52:31,258
well, we were picking stuff up in class

756
00:52:31,258 --> 00:52:34,258
and we were doing this until finally

757
00:52:34,258 --> 00:52:36,258
it seemed like a revelation

758
00:52:36,258 --> 00:52:39,758
that what has been said

759
00:52:39,758 --> 00:52:43,258
in the classical teaching of it,

760
00:52:43,258 --> 00:52:48,258
which of course in modern society is rejected,

761
00:52:48,258 --> 00:52:50,258
happens to be the case.

762
00:52:50,258 --> 00:52:54,258
And I said, this has to be seen.

763
00:52:54,258 --> 00:52:56,258
Seen, what?

764
00:52:56,258 --> 00:52:58,258
This is what you mean.

765
00:52:58,258 --> 00:53:01,258
Of course, of course.

766
00:53:02,258 --> 00:53:08,258
But we're back to that step there.

767
00:53:08,258 --> 00:53:11,258
Why was that person,

768
00:53:11,258 --> 00:53:15,258
and so many other students following suit,

769
00:53:15,258 --> 00:53:23,258
anguished at the point where the practical issue arose?

770
00:53:23,258 --> 00:53:30,258
There was a feeling, I suppose,

771
00:53:30,258 --> 00:53:33,258
that they were on the cliff.

772
00:53:33,258 --> 00:53:35,258
Quite, quite.

773
00:53:35,258 --> 00:53:41,258
And naturally alertness was required,

774
00:53:41,258 --> 00:53:46,258
but alertness registers that we're on a cliff.

775
00:53:46,258 --> 00:53:47,258
Quite.

776
00:53:47,258 --> 00:53:48,758
So therefore the best thing to

777
00:53:48,758 --> 00:53:50,258
do is turn around and run back.

778
00:53:50,258 --> 00:53:54,258
Yes, yes.

779
00:53:54,258 --> 00:53:59,258
Sir, I think you see,

780
00:53:59,258 --> 00:54:05,258
we are so caught up in words.

781
00:54:05,258 --> 00:54:12,258
To us the word is not the thing.

782
00:54:12,258 --> 00:54:16,258
The description is not the description.

783
00:54:16,258 --> 00:54:17,258
Not described.

784
00:54:17,258 --> 00:54:22,258
To us the description is all that matters.

785
00:54:23,258 --> 00:54:26,258
Because we are slaves to words.

786
00:54:26,258 --> 00:54:27,258
And to ritual.

787
00:54:27,258 --> 00:54:29,258
Ritual and all the rest of it.

788
00:54:29,258 --> 00:54:31,258
So when you say,

789
00:54:31,258 --> 00:54:37,258
look, the thing matters more than the word,

790
00:54:37,258 --> 00:54:40,258
and then they say, how am

791
00:54:40,258 --> 00:54:43,258
I to get rid of the word?

792
00:54:43,258 --> 00:54:45,258
How am I to communicate if I have no word?

793
00:54:45,258 --> 00:54:47,258
You see how they've gone off?

794
00:54:47,258 --> 00:54:52,258
They're not concerned with the thing, but with the word.

795
00:54:52,258 --> 00:54:54,258
Yes.

796
00:54:54,258 --> 00:54:59,258
The door is not the word.

797
00:54:59,258 --> 00:55:03,258
So when you are caught up in words,

798
00:55:03,258 --> 00:55:10,258
the word door becomes extraordinarily important.

799
00:55:10,258 --> 00:55:13,258
And not the door.

800
00:55:13,258 --> 00:55:14,758
And I don't really need to

801
00:55:14,758 --> 00:55:16,258
come to terms with the door,

802
00:55:16,258 --> 00:55:20,258
I say to myself, because I have the word.

803
00:55:20,258 --> 00:55:21,258
Exactly.

804
00:55:21,258 --> 00:55:23,258
I have it all.

805
00:55:23,258 --> 00:55:30,258
So education has done this.

806
00:55:30,258 --> 00:55:33,258
A great part of this

807
00:55:33,258 --> 00:55:36,258
education is the acceptance of words

808
00:55:37,258 --> 00:55:43,258
as an abstraction from the fact, from the what is.

809
00:55:43,258 --> 00:55:48,258
All philosophies are based on that.

810
00:55:48,258 --> 00:55:51,258
Theorise, theorise, theorise endlessly,

811
00:55:51,258 --> 00:55:53,258
how one should live.

812
00:55:53,258 --> 00:55:58,258
And the philosopher himself doesn't live.

813
00:55:58,258 --> 00:56:00,258
You see this all over.

814
00:56:00,258 --> 00:56:02,258
A. Yes, I know, especially some philosophies

815
00:56:02,258 --> 00:56:06,258
that have seemed to me quite bizarre in this respect.

816
00:56:06,258 --> 00:56:09,258
I've asked my colleagues from time to time,

817
00:56:09,258 --> 00:56:12,258
well, if you believe that

818
00:56:12,258 --> 00:56:15,258
stuff, why don't you do it?

819
00:56:15,258 --> 00:56:16,758
And they look at me as

820
00:56:16,758 --> 00:56:18,258
though I'm out of my mind,

821
00:56:18,258 --> 00:56:22,258
as though nobody would really seriously ask that question.

822
00:56:22,258 --> 00:56:24,258
But if you can't ask that question,

823
00:56:24,258 --> 00:56:26,258
well, what question is worth asking?

824
00:56:26,258 --> 00:56:27,258
Quite right.

825
00:56:27,258 --> 00:56:28,258
Yes.

826
00:56:28,258 --> 00:56:31,258
A. I was thinking about that marvellous story

827
00:56:31,258 --> 00:56:36,258
you told in our previous conversation about the monkey

828
00:56:36,258 --> 00:56:41,258
while you were speaking about this.

829
00:56:41,258 --> 00:56:45,258
When she shook hands with you,

830
00:56:45,258 --> 00:56:49,258
nobody had told her how to shake hands.

831
00:56:49,258 --> 00:56:50,258
K. No, it stretched out.

832
00:56:50,258 --> 00:56:51,258
A. Yes.

833
00:56:51,258 --> 00:56:54,258
K. When I took it.

834
00:56:54,258 --> 00:56:56,258
A. Wasn't something that she was taught how to do

835
00:56:56,258 --> 00:56:58,258
through a verbal communication.

836
00:56:58,258 --> 00:57:02,258
It was the appropriate thing at the time

837
00:57:02,258 --> 00:57:05,258
without anyone measuring its appropriateness.

838
00:57:05,258 --> 00:57:06,258
K. Quite.

839
00:57:06,258 --> 00:57:11,258
A. Isn't that something?

840
00:57:11,258 --> 00:57:18,258
A. Yes.

841
00:57:18,258 --> 00:57:21,258
I can't tell you how grateful I am

842
00:57:21,258 --> 00:57:27,258
to have been able to share this with you.

843
00:57:27,258 --> 00:57:31,758
I've seen in respect to

844
00:57:31,758 --> 00:57:36,258
my own activity as a teacher

845
00:57:36,258 --> 00:57:45,258
where I must perform therapy even on my language

846
00:57:45,258 --> 00:57:48,758
so that I don't give

847
00:57:48,758 --> 00:57:52,258
the student an occasion for thinking

848
00:57:52,258 --> 00:57:57,258
that I am simply adding to this endless chain,

849
00:57:57,258 --> 00:58:02,258
link after link after link.

850
00:58:02,258 --> 00:58:04,258
There are two therapies here then.

851
00:58:04,258 --> 00:58:09,258
There's the therapy that relates to words

852
00:58:09,258 --> 00:58:14,258
and that flows out naturally.

853
00:58:14,258 --> 00:58:15,258
It's not a contrivance.

854
00:58:15,258 --> 00:58:19,258
It flows out naturally, if I've understood you correctly,

855
00:58:19,258 --> 00:58:25,258
from the therapy within.

856
00:58:25,258 --> 00:58:29,258
Now this relates directly, as you were saying earlier,

857
00:58:29,258 --> 00:58:32,258
to meditation. Are we ready?

858
00:58:32,258 --> 00:58:34,258
K. I think that's too complicated.

859
00:58:34,258 --> 00:58:36,258
A. I don't mean right now,

860
00:58:36,258 --> 00:58:39,258
but maybe in one of our next conversations we could...

861
00:58:39,258 --> 00:58:42,258
K. We must discuss several things here, sir.

862
00:58:42,258 --> 00:58:45,258
What is love, what is death, what is meditation,

863
00:58:45,258 --> 00:58:48,258
what is the whole movement of living?

864
00:58:48,258 --> 00:58:49,258
We've got a great deal to do.

865
00:58:49,258 --> 00:58:50,758
A. Oh, I do look

866
00:58:50,758 --> 00:58:52,258
forward very much to that. Splendid.

